 "description": "March 11, 2013: Bitcoin split into two chains.\nThe new version 0.8 accepted a huge block (block 225,430, over 5,000 transactions). Older versions couldn't read it - their database ran out of locks. Mt. Gox and BitPay paused deposits and the price dropped 24%.\nDevelopers chose the old chain, big mining pools downgraded, and about six hours later the chains joined again. 24 blocks were wiped out, and a $10,000 double spend hit OKPay.\n\nBug or warning? \ud83d\udc47\n\nNot financial advice. Entertainment and education only.",
